bench_loop_nested — 20% without BTB vs 73% with BTB

outer = 5, inner = 5
outer_loop:
  inner_loop:
    inner--
    BNE inner, 0, inner_loop   ← taken 4 times, not-taken 1 time per outer iteration
  outer--
  BNE outer, 0, outer_loop     ← taken 4 times, not-taken once total


Without BTB (24 mispredictions out of 30):

Every taken branch is wrong → 5×4 inner + 4 outer = 24 mispredictions


With BTB (8 mispredictions out of 30):

Inner loop: 5 outer iterations × 1 first-miss + 5 exit mispredictions = ~8 mispredictions
The BTB remembers both branches across outer iterations